# CREDITS — One Ember

A 38-second film in the Woodcut Print style, made entirely in code.
The kiln, the potter and the story are invented. No real workshop or person is portrayed.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English. Model and engine
are released under the licences of the kokoro-onnx project
(https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx). Offline synthesis.

## Music
Original score, synthesised for this film (`music/score.py`).
No sample library. Contrabass drone, cello spiccato, woodblock, frame drum,
one tam-tam and one struck-metal note are numpy synthesis.

## Typefaces
- Cormorant Garamond — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (Catharsis Fonts); see `fonts/OFL.txt`
  Copied from the Impasto demo's font set. Used as the letterpress face.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn with this film's knife and print compositor (`engine/woodcut.js`).
No stock footage, no photographs, no third-party images.

## Sound effects
All foley is synthesised for this film (`mix.py`): room hush, knife, chips, ember
crackle, a wood strike, brayer, baren, paper and the peel.
